<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	Decision (Plan 4a Task 10): this app is NOT sandboxed.

	Rationale: personal project distributed outside the Mac App Store; running
	unsandboxed simplifies Plan 4b's sound-effect playback and save/export
	paths (no security-scoped bookmarks, no entitlement plumbing for
	arbitrary file access) at essentially zero cost given there is no App
	Store submission planned. Revisit only if MAS distribution becomes a goal.

	Because the app is not sandboxed, App Sandbox entitlements
	(com.apple.security.app-sandbox, .network.client, etc.) are intentionally
	omitted — an unsandboxed process already has the network/file access it
	needs. This file is kept (rather than deleted) as the recorded decision
	and as a ready slot if sandboxing is revisited later.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
